mythicbotany.lexicon.page.alfsteel.0=Alfsteel armor uses the 1.12.2 ItemArmor texture callback and the alfsteel_0 and alfsteel_1 armor layers.
mythicbotany.lexicon.page.alfsteel.1=A complete set grants the protection and combat effects implemented by the port.
mythicbotany.lexicon.page.alfsteel.2=Keep the armor texture files under assets/mythicbotany/textures/model.
mythicbotany.lexicon.page.infuser.0=The Mana Infuser consumes mana from its internal receiver and applies the JSON recipes in the MythicBotany recipe resources.
mythicbotany.lexicon.page.infuser.1=Place an input in the infuser and provide enough mana for the selected infusion.
mythicbotany.lexicon.page.mana.0=The greatest mana ring is a Baubles ring and implements Botania's IManaItem API. It can receive and export mana through pools and other mana items.
mythicbotany.lexicon.page.mana.1=Mana is stored in the item NBT key mana and is shown with Botania's standard mana tooltip.
mythicbotany.lexicon.page.overview.0=MythicBotany extends Botania with Alfheim magic, world runes, Alfsteel and new mana devices.<br>All entries in this section use the Botania 1.12.2 Lexicon API.
mythicbotany.lexicon.page.overview.1=Use Botania mana infrastructure together with the devices and rituals described in this section.
mythicbotany.lexicon.page.pixie.0=The Alf Pixie can be created with /summon mythicbotany:alf_pixie or with its spawn egg.
mythicbotany.lexicon.page.pixie.1=The spawn egg supports both air use and block use and only consumes an egg after the entity is accepted by the world.
mythicbotany.lexicon.page.pylon.0=The Alfsteel Pylon is a high-tier mana device from Alfheim.
mythicbotany.lexicon.page.pylon.1=Its recipe and behaviour are defined by the 1.12.2 port.
mythicbotany.lexicon.page.rings.0=Mythic rings are Baubles-compatible accessories. Their effects are applied while worn.
mythicbotany.lexicon.page.rings.1=The mana-bearing rings use Botania's 1.12.2 mana interfaces.
mythicbotany.lexicon.page.runes.0=World runes are used by the rune rituals in the JSON recipe resources.
mythicbotany.lexicon.page.runes.1=Ritual positions are relative to the central holder and rotate with the ritual.
